          "headline": "Philippines enters World Bank’s upper-middle-income group",
          "headlineHref": "/interactive-timeline/index.html?date=2026-07-01&search=Philippines%20enters%20World%20Bank%E2%80%99s%20upper-middle-income%20group",
          "descriptionHtml": "<p>The World Bank’s annual classification moved the Philippines into the upper-middle-income group, with the government welcoming the change on July 2. The classification reflects national income per person, rather than a guarantee that individual households have become middle class. The milestone sharpened the question of how economic gains translate into jobs and family purchasing power.</p>",
